+# N24 closed Dev controller v1
+
+This is CPU-prepared infrastructure, not execution authority. Frozen science is Phase A commit `3f6db2dc3dcc8db45b66a649568b43248c8b5f0e`; original numerical backend proof and frozen runtime come from the SHA-bound N23 plan at source `51104470983cdbafd08feb87f2f39b7553779405`. The scientific protocol remains SHA256 `77163171815bdade8d05a4010ff59aa24a4157d447d6d7fb430f3163a80c4b3b`.
+
+The matrix is task-major tasks 0..9 × C0/Q0/N23/N24. All original Dev seed/init/BDDL rows are copied; N23 is an ablation comparator only. All 40 first-valid cells and candidate >=5/10 and >=each comparator, plus substantive QD/ED, are required for promotion. No rescue-count minimum. Numeric futility is checked only after complete accepted quadruples. Incomplete prefixes keep their actual denominators. No validation/formal launcher is provided.
+
+There are at most 40 primary plus two completed, sole-Codex-timeout whole-episode recoveries, at most one per cell. Exact existing classifier gates apply equally to all arms. A failed recovery, valid task failure, native error, missing data, other API error, process interruption or whole-worker timeout is never retried. Invalid originals and their costs remain; unknown token usage stays unknown/partial. Local ceiling22 GPU hours, 1800s whole worker plus40s termination per episode. Cumulative caps478/100h and buckets51/187/180/40/20 with32h validation/12h formal reservations are unchanged. This implementation explicitly keeps the optional <=60s tensor preflight CLOSED; source-equivalence review is its only admission path. No previous preflight authority is reused.
+
+Every arm uses the original wrapper process around main.py, including native audit before exit. N23 and N24 audit arithmetic uses assigned CUDA inside that process; C0/Q0 use CPU arithmetic. The wrapper retains historical `n23-*` context/receipt filenames and schemas as shared infrastructure. New N24 plan routing is explicit. The only modified wrapper bodies are validate_context, run_worker, verify_receipt. Other functions and original numerical files stay byte-identical. Supervisors consume hashed JSON receipts, never rerun CUDA audit.
+
+N24 native gates are profile-bound: deleting every N24 marker cannot downgrade a guided episode to N23. Real EDSChunkMetrics provider/default omission is accepted for C0/Q0. No metrics file is legal only with independent native canonical count0 and episode_compute.policy_counters_available=true/guided_chunks0 and matching terminal guided count. N24 guided metrics bind11/176/10, cache updates, substitutions, original archive slots, and actual parent sources/cells. `cache_updates` counts canonical batches in which the cache's best entry changes; it is not the number of within-batch row assignments. Original archive metadata never claims a rescued nonmember as an archive member. Aux overhead and other measured costs are retained.
+
+Source/review closure:
+
+1. Root integrates the exact reviewed commit into owning study_worktree under idle private ownership. `worker.source_record(root, contract.source_paths(vars(runner)))` records commit and sorted actual file bytes, including all214 historical scientific/controller dependencies and N24 additions.
+2. Root calls `bridge.build(source, contract.runtime_ref(), root)` and writes once to variant/source-equivalence-bridge-v1.json. The helper checks science against Phase A, original unchanged numerical files against511, restricted controller delta, and all unchanged wrapper function bodies. Changed wrapper bodies have explicit old/new hashes for root review. The bridge references original settled strict176-batch+FP32/BF16 proof and Phase A CPU evidence; admission rechecks original proof/report/process against private terminal ledger. No source-embedded final review/proof hash creates a circular freeze.
+3. Root writes exact `n24-source-runtime-review-v1` at final-source-runtime-review-v1.json. Keys: schema, disposition='accepted', source(full record), runtime(ref), protocol(ref), source_plan(ref), source_bridge(ref), native_preflight={required:false,proof:null}, no_gpu_release=true. All byte refs are actual path/SHA.
+4. Root writes exact `n24-dev-authority-v1` at adoption-v1/authority.json. Keys: schema, cohort_id, source, runtime, protocol, final_review(ref), limits(contract.LIMITS), caps(contract.CAPS), recorded_at(nonempty), authority_interpretation(nonempty), validation_authorized=false, formal_authorized=false. Under existing private locks root adopts only its ref as state.n24_dev_authority; no budget increase or old binding rewrite is required. CPU executor does not do this.
+5. `python scripts/qd_ed_n24_prepare.py --output VARIANT/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --freeze` checks exact source/review/adoption/private resource/settled ledger/full remaining capacity/runtime before freezing. Root then reviews original Hydra arguments and Codex-only managed-login transport. Draft command without --freeze remains non-executable with null review/authority.
+6. Root writes exact execution-release-v1.json: schema='n24-dev-execution-release-v1', plan(ref), source_commit, cohort_id, episode_keys(all40 exact order), authority(ref), physical_gpu7, limits, validation_authorized=false, formal_authorized=false. No source or profile change after review/freeze.
+7. Only root starts `python scripts/qd_ed_n24_supervise.py --plan VARIANT/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --release VARIANT/execution-release-v1.json --status VARIANT/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. It requires no prior N24 reservation/status/result and exclusive controller lock; original runner locks, actual GPU UUID/free-device checks and append-only costs govern every dispatch. Never auto-relaunch.
+
+Terminal result-v1.json and execution/terminal-ledger-v1.json are immutable, automatically produced in controller finally from this cohort's private events and independently checked receipt/terminal bindings. Successful terminal statuses must agree with independently reconstructed prefix/gates. If a valid attempt was journaled before controller progress persistence failed, keep both controller and journal prefixes, all valid outcomes/costs, and mark INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED; never silently promote or resume. Missing/mismatched status likewise cannot authorize promotion. The ledger snapshot contains only N24 Dev events; protected outcomes are neither read for tuning nor exposed.
+
+All online Stage calls remain current managed Codex login, chatgpt/gpt-6-astra/low/E2/180s. Poe and fallback remain prohibited; no credentials are copied or inspected. Tests are synthetic with two CPU threads, invisible CUDA, blocked dispatch/network/actual historical artifacts. Source-equivalence and CPU evidence are not a benchmark score: N24 score remains Unknown until actual authorized Dev.
+
+N24-only zero-guided timeout evidence compatibility: the unchanged old diagnose function also packages evidence files. For an absent metrics file only, N24 executes a private function with the exact original code object and globals copied with exactly evidence_files replaced. No module global, timeout_event, diagnose bytecode or derivative gate changes. Independent native canonical count0, episode-compute guided0 and terminal guided0 must all be known exact integers (booleans/Unknown rejected). The private reader binds metrics absence as present:false/sha256:null; all other mandatory files stay hashed, and optional no-event safety retains its old convention. Eligibility reconstruction rejects later metrics presence. Ordinary present-file cases call original diagnose directly. This is serialized evidence compatibility, not a new recoverable error type.
+
+The eligibility explicitly binds evidence_packaging_reader (N24 source path/SHA) and packaging mode; diagnostic.diagnostic_reader still identifies the original unchanged transport diagnostic code. Private clone preserves code/defaults/keyword-only defaults/closure; no shared-global substitution occurs.
